      <P><FONT face=3DVerdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif color=3D#ffffff =
size=3D2>
      <DIV>
      <DL>
        <DT>11/29/03=20
        <DD>Drew a schematic of all the TTY connections, similar to =
"Figure=20
        5-7", but with more detail and as many parts values as I =
currently know.=20
        Still need to know the resistance of the reader-run relay to be =
able to=20
        design a reliable replacement.
        <P></P>
        <DT>11/28/03=20
        <DD>Tried to fix my second M706. Replaced the first FF in the =
divider=20
        chain, but the clocking is still dead. Guess I'll have to =
replace the=20
        second, too.
        <P></P>
        <DD>Found out why my TTY printer is dead. The "Carriage Rear =
Rail" has=20
        fallen off of it's mounting screws.
        <P></P>
        <DD>Filled up my JameCo shopping cart with parts for the M452 =
and W076=20
        replacements. Always a shock when so many little bitty items add =
up to=20
        real money.
        <P></P>
        <DT>11/25/03=20
        <DD>Fiddled with a new design for reader-run. I still haven't =
figured=20
        out a way to supply the needed drive, keep the component count =
down, and=20
        not add load to the reader-run line.
        <P></P>
        <DT>11/25/03=20
        <DD>Just to prove I could do it, I downloaded Focal '69 at 19200 =
baud.=20
        It took 6 seconds, and gave a zero checksum. Wish my 8L worked =
well=20
        enough to actually *run* Focal '69. Guess now I can download and =
run=20
        some diagnostics to figure out what is wrong, though.
        <P></P>
        <DT>11/24/03=20
        <DD>Checked out the RS-232 side of the W076X -- it works. =
Shortened the=20
        pulse length of the one-shot in the M452X and that got the input =
side=20
        working at 110 baud (output worked before). Tried setting 19200 =
baud,=20
        but it didn't work. Eventually discovered I had swapped the =
wiring for=20
        19200 baud and 4800 baud. It works fine now at all the speeds =
(up to=20
        19200) that I can set with Hypterterm. So nice to use reliable =
RS-232=20
        stuff instead of my half-dead TTY.
        <P></P>
        <DD>My cable for the LA36 finally arrived. Idiot seller sent it =
media=20
        rate. Since when is a cable media?? Two months to get it here.
        <P></P>
        <DT>11/23/03=20
        <DD>Spent a bunch of time converting this stuff into web pages =
so others=20
        can see it.
        <P></P>
        <DD>Started this log. Typed up a "To Do" list, indicating what =
needs to=20
        be done for the major hardware pieces in the collection.
        <P></P>
        <DT>11/22/03=20
        <DD>Tracked the problem with the W076X to the BC05M cable I =
built, which=20
        is now fixed. TTY input works. TTY is in such bad shape that I =
can=92t see=20
        the echo, but the print mechanism is activated correctly. Will =
have to=20
        switch to LA36 when connectors get here. Still no ability to =
test=20
        reader-run in real use.
        <P></P>
        <DD>Spent some time writing a documentation-sheet for the W076X =
to match=20
        the one for the M452X.
        <P></P>
        <DD>Spent some time getting the W076 board description ready for =
the=20
        board fabricator.
        <P></P>
        <DT>11/21/03=20
        <DD>Built BC05M equivalent cable for testing W076X. W076X =
isn=92t working=20
        =96 only 2ma is available at the transmit loop, instead of 20ma. =
Odd,=20
        since everything checks out when I measure it at the chips on =
the W076X.
        <P></P>
        <DT>11/20/03=20
        <DD>Convinced myself to stop fiddling with the M452X for now and =
work on=20
        the W076X. Still need to check frequencies against my M410s, and =
to=20
        decide whether or not to rework the monostable to match DEC=92s =
design.
        <P></P></DD></DL><!--"''"--></DIV></FONT>
